                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0398538e-decf-3921-8729-41438f36cf3e",
                        "entry_id": "f8b62a65-d224-3d42-93d6-7790e26b3ef7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "кулин. разновидность соуса (майонез с каперсами и горчицей)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "51292714-0fe1-4b3f-a903-b9d69c09e1ed",
                                "sense_id": "0398538e-decf-3921-8729-41438f36cf3e",
                                "text": "И ещё осмелюсь спросить, ваше сиятельство, какой соус прикажете подавать к петуху: тартар или польский, а то можно просто сухари в масле?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "90f73f89-62e9-3c38-8620-795ff5fdb354",
                "word": "тартар",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "42d85677-ec7e-375f-9e4f-c52ea7eab464",
                        "entry_id": "90f73f89-62e9-3c38-8620-795ff5fdb354",
                        "glosses": [
                            "житель Тартарии"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "76e4a27d-e630-4f17-8719-ec2f66b3c55e",
                                "sense_id": "42d85677-ec7e-375f-9e4f-c52ea7eab464",
                                "text": "Была Европа да кончилась, стал вместо неё Тартар и жители её теперь были тартары."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "c744ac80-f3ee-3850-889a-3b0b751f84bc",
                "word": "Тартар",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f7e9339-1b32-39c2-a65d-6e01bffcb2fa",
                        "entry_id": "c744ac80-f3ee-3850-889a-3b0b751f84bc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "(в древнегреческой мифологии) глубочайшая бездна, находящаяся под царством Аида"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c22b16c-2ee7-44bf-8f57-1d2f4231c160",
                                "sense_id": "2f7e9339-1b32-39c2-a65d-6e01bffcb2fa",
                                "text": "Древние греки считали, что медная наковальня летела бы от поверхности земли до Тартара целых девять дней."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b5334ae2-3764-491f-bde8-0d72c9dd23f1",
                        "source_entry_id": "c744ac80-f3ee-3850-889a-3b0b751f84bc",
                        "source_sense_id": "2f7e9339-1b32-39c2-a65d-6e01bffcb2fa",
                        "target_lang_word": "Tartarus",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Tartarus",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a5eaa7d2-da96-3194-8a4b-be1ef8eedb93",
                                        "entry_id": "277b394b-e57d-36bd-bedd-1e4a2b9a9fff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dark and gloomy part of the realm of Hades, reserved for the damned and the wicked, such as the Titans; an equivalent of hell in Greek and Roman mythology."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Greek",
                                            "Roman"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c934370-ab41-4a5a-b9b1-ecfdb6640c9a",
                                                "sense_id": "a5eaa7d2-da96-3194-8a4b-be1ef8eedb93",
                                                "text": "[…] them with Fire and hoſtile Arms / Fearleſs aſſault, and to the brow of Heav'n / Purſuing, drive them out from God and bliſs, / Into thir place of puniſhment, the Gulf / Of Tartarus, which ready opens wide / His fiery Chaos to receave thir fall."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46fb987d-7ca2-3c30-bc27-86db062c4591",
                                        "entry_id": "277b394b-e57d-36bd-bedd-1e4a2b9a9fff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any hellish place; a dark gloomy chasm or pit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71fec39e-2930-4d1f-8e3c-c688b1077a67",
                                                "sense_id": "46fb987d-7ca2-3c30-bc27-86db062c4591",
                                                "text": "We lay there hour after hour in terror and misery of mind so deep that I will not attempt to describe it, and listened to the wild storm-voices of that Tartarus, as, set to the deep undertone of the spur opposite against which the wind hummed like some awful harp, they called to each other from precipice to precipice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e83f1c91-ec1e-4a10-a25c-94340d123894",
                                                "sense_id": "46fb987d-7ca2-3c30-bc27-86db062c4591",
                                                "text": "After arranging a rendezvous, we separate. Mattie and Liz go off in one direction, and Em and I in another. From this our progress seems like a descent into Tartarus. Em pauses before a miserable-looking saloon, pushes open the low, swinging door, and we go in."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
